Data Analytics & Business Automation Portfolio
Welcome to my technical repository. This project serves as the backend documentation and code repository for the business solutions showcased in my Notion Portfolio.

Repository Overview

This repository contains the technical logic, database schemas, and automation scripts used to build end-to-end data solutions for the Facilities Management (FM) and Procurement sectors.

Project Highlights

01 | Procurement & Fleet Analytics (Power BI & ETL)
Folder: /01_Procurement_Fleet_Analytics
This project focuses on advanced ETL processes to unify disparate fleet data and procurement records.
- SQL Schema: Includes the DDL for the ProcRep fact table.
- Power Query (M Code) Transformation:
    Standardized four distinct data sources (Fuel, Toll, Parking, EV) by renaming headers and enforcing strict data types.
    Implemented custom M logic to handle currency conversion for EV charging data, stripping currency symbols and applying a fixed 1.20 exchange rate.
    Automated data pruning by removing unnecessary columns and retaining only "Date", "Category", and "Total Cost (EUR)".
    Utilized "Append Queries" to stack standardized tables into a unified Master Fleet Costs table.
Performance Optimization: Configured staging queries to refresh in the background without loading into the final report model to minimize memory footprint.

02 | BMS Automated Pricing Tool (MS Access & VBA)
Folder: /02_BMS_Pricing_Tool
A relational database application built to automate complex engineering estimations.
- RDBMS Design: Features the relational structure connecting master supplier libraries to project-specific cost calculations.
- VBA automation: Script for automating the export of professional Bill of Quantities (BOQ) and Quotations to PDF.


🛠️ Technical Stack
Languages: SQL (T-SQL/MySQL), VBA, M (Power Query), DAX.

Tools: Power BI Desktop, Microsoft Access, Excel Online, SharePoint.

Methodologies: Star Schema Modeling, RDBMS Design, Agile Process Improvement.

